# A compact branch window taken from a real C674x image: a 16-bit bnop issuing
# with a 32-bit load and move. Decoding a compact slot as if it were 32 bits
# yields an unrelated instruction, so this covers the path the hand-written
# 32-bit cases cannot reach. The bnop is taken, which leaves the load and the
# branch in its delay slot predicated off: untaken, that branch would issue
# inside the window, which a window does not model.
NAME=c6x a compact branch window from real firmware
FILE=malloc://256
CMDS=<<EOF
e analysis.arch=tms320
e cfg.bigendian=false
e analysis.cpu=c674x
e asm.cpu=c674x
e scr.color=0
